  "body": "Fixes #7771.\n\n## What\n\n`count_periods`' `Period::Week` branch in `pkgs/id/src/didit/eval.rs` used unchecked `NaiveDate - Duration` / `NaiveDate + Duration` arithmetic, which **panics** at the calendar boundary (chrono implements those operators via `expect`). The `Day` branch answers `EvalError::OutOfRange` for the same instants (`succ_opt`/`pred_opt`), and the `Custom` branch was converted to checked arithmetic in #7766 — whose comment incorrectly claimed the Week branch was calendar-guarded. Residual of #7766.\n\n- Week branch: Monday offset, `monday + 7 days`, and `monday - 7 days` now use `checked_sub_signed` / `checked_add_signed`, mapping `None` to `EvalError::OutOfRange`.\n- `resolve_local`: the `naive + Duration::hours(1)` DST-gap shift is now `checked_add_signed`; an unrepresentable shift falls through to the existing UTC interpretation instead of panicking.\n- The #7766 comment in the `Custom` branch no longer claims the Week branch gets its ruling \"from the calendar\".\n- Regression test `week_period_at_calendar_boundary_is_out_of_range_not_a_panic` mirrors the #7766 Custom test: a Week expectation (`ActiveWindow::Always`, UTC) evaluated at noon on `NaiveDate::MAX` and `NaiveDate::MIN` returns `Err(EvalError::OutOfRange)`; an ordinary week still evaluates.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Probe (pre-fix, laptop, verbatim branch code, chrono 0.4.45, release build) `~/git/fleet/probe-didit-week-overflow`: Week **panics** at both boundary instants; Day returns `Err(OutOfRange)`; ordinary controls pass.\n- New regression test panics pre-fix (same probe arithmetic) and passes with this change.\n- `cargo test --lib didit::` on the laptop: see PR checks / agent note on #7771 for the result.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796752643&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7773&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7773&signature=b0abcb0152f794fa0939dc0d7f54580c138dc65357b4f8e6b8fc80afdbb77d5b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7773?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
